[h1]Train Cargo Tools[/h1]
Trains are able to accept shapes and fluids and put them into packages, but they only stay in packages while on the train.
What if you could package things into train cargo wherever you wanted? 

Pack shapes or fluids into cargo containers, carry them on a cargo belt, buffer them in a cargo store, and unpack them where you need them.
Train stations will accept the containers straight from a belt, so a station no longer has to be the only place cargo exists.

[h2]What you get[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Shape and Fluid Cargo Packagers[/b] - Package 360 shapes or 60L of fluid into cargo containers!
[*][b]Shape and Fluid Cargo Unpackagers[/b] - Unpack the contents of the container back onto a space belt or pipe!
[*][b]Cargo Belts[/b] - Transport your cargo bundles without needing trains!
[*][b]Cargo Stores[/b] - Buffer up to 75 cargo of any type
[/list]

All of the content in this mod is gated behind a research unlock titled "Cargo Machines", as well as a second unlock for "Cargo Stores".
Once unlocked, find all cargo related tools in the hotbar, and view the wiki pages which explain each added building and how to use it!

[h2]Before you install[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]This mod affects save games.[/b] Once you install it to a save, you cannot play that save without it.
[*]Requires Shapez Shifter.
[/list]

